troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting#network-and-proxies","content":"A malformed proxy URL in the environment makes requests fail rather than being ignored.","locale":"en"},"8282":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting-118","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting#network-and-proxies","content":"`network.system_proxy` only works on Windows.","locale":"en"},"8283":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting-119","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting#network-and-proxies","content":"SOCKS proxies do not apply to Bedrock's AWS SDK; Bedrock needs an HTTP(S) proxy.","locale":"en"},"8284":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting-120","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting#network-and-proxies","content":"Local addresses (such as a local Ollama) always go direct, never through a proxy.","locale":"en"},"8285":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting-121","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting#network-and-proxies","content":"Configuration is covered in Network and proxies.","locale":"en"},"8286":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting-122","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting#stations-refusing-images-or-tools","content":"When a model cannot read images (`vision` is `false` in its capabilities), the Playground has the **Image model** (`playground.vision_model`) describe the image in words first, and says above the reply **The image “…” was described by …, because this model can’t read images.** When no model can read it, or the **Image model** is **Off**, it says **The image “…” was left out: no model could read it.**","locale":"en"},"8287":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting-123","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting#stations-refusing-images-or-tools","content":"When a model should read images but the upstream refuses the image before the reply starts (an error mentioning image, vision, multimodal and the like), the Playground retries once with descriptions and says **… refused the image, so it was sent as a description.**","locale":"en"},"8288":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting-124","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting#stations-refusing-images-or-tools","content":"Over the API, the gateway does no such conversion and the upstream's error comes back as is. To send images, pick a model whose `vision` is `true`.","locale":"en"},"8289":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting-125","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting#stations-refusing-images-or-tools","content":"When a model does not support tool calls, or the upstream refuses `tools` before the reply starts (an error mentioning tool, tool_choice or function call), the Playground retries without tools and says **… can’t call tools, so it answered without them.** Pick a model that supports tools (**Tools** on the **Models** page). Turning tools on and the approval modes are covered in Playground tools.","locale":"en"},"8290":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting-126","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting#stations-refusing-images-or-tools","content":"Over the API, an upstream's refusal of `tools` is returned to the client as is.","locale":"en"},"8291":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting-127","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting#data-and-files","content":"`hoshimi.db` was used by a newer Hoshimi and an older one is running now. It still runs, but some records may not show correctly. Upgrade, or restore the data directory from a backup.","locale":"en"},"8292":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting-128","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting#data-and-files","content":"`hoshimi config set` and hand edits need a server restart. More importantly, while the server runs, every settings save in the Web UI, every login and every renewal writes the in-memory configuration back to `config.json`, overwriting changes made to the file in the meantime. Stop the server before changing the file.","locale":"en"},"8293":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting-129","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting#data-and-files","content":"When old JSON records were imported after an upgrade, this file could not be read; it was renamed aside and that record started empty. Nothing else is affected; delete it if you do not need it.","locale":"en"},"8294":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting-130","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-troubleshooting#data-and-files","content":"If the problem remains, open a report on GitHub Issues with logs taken with `HOSHIMI_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG`, the output of `hoshimi version` and the steps to reproduce. Logs can contain account ids and host names; check them before sharing.","locale":"en"},"8295":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","type":"page","content":"Usage statistics","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Advanced"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","locale":"en"},"8296":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-0","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","content":"How the gateway records each call: which fields, where token and cache counts come from, how speed is measured, how long 