ult 50","locale":"en"},"8419":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-123","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-call-list","content":"`before`","locale":"en"},"8420":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-124","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-call-list","content":"The previous page's `next`, for older calls","locale":"en"},"8421":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-125","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-call-list","content":"`model`, `provider`, `origin`","locale":"en"},"8422":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-126","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-call-list","content":"Filter by field","locale":"en"},"8423":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-127","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-call-list","content":"`account`","locale":"en"},"8424":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-128","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-call-list","content":"An account id, or `channel/account`","locale":"en"},"8425":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-129","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-call-list","content":"`ok`","locale":"en"},"8426":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-130","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-call-list","content":"`true` for successes only, `false` for failures only","locale":"en"},"8427":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-131","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-call-list","content":"`since`, `until`","locale":"en"},"8428":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-132","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-call-list","content":"ISO 8601 times; without an offset, server local time; `until` is exclusive","locale":"en"},"8429":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-133","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-call-list","content":"`q`","locale":"en"},"8430":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-134","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-call-list","content":"Case-insensitive text in the model, channel, account, error code, error message or finish reason","locale":"en"},"8431":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-135","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-call-list","content":"Every record has a sequence number `seq` that never repeats, even after the statistics are cleared, so it is safe as a paging cursor.","locale":"en"},"8432":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-136","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#clearing","content":"**Reset statistics** on the Web UI's **Usage** page, or:","locale":"en"},"8433":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-137","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#clearing","content":"Every counter, chart and call record is cleared; this cannot be undone. Calls in flight are still recorded when they end.","locale":"en"},"8434":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-138","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-live-view","content":"The **Live activity** panel in the top bar shows the calls in flight (**Waiting**, **Thinking**, **Answering**, **Calling tools**), today's totals and the calls that just finished. It reads a server-sent event stream:","locale":"en"},"8435":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-139","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-live-view","content":"Each frame is `data: <JSON>`, told apart by `type`:","locale":"en"},"8436":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-140","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-live-view","content":"`type`","locale":"en"},"8437":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-141","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-live-view","content":"Contents","locale":"en"},"8438":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-142","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-live-view","content":"`snapshot`","locale":"en"},"8439":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-143","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-live-view","content":"The first frame after connecting: server time, the calls in flight, today's totals, the latest finished calls","locale":"en"},"8440":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-144","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-live-view","content":"`started`","locale":"en"},"8441":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-145","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-live-view","content":"A call started","locale":"en"},"8442":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-146","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-live-view","content":"`progress`","locale":"en"},"8443":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-147","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-live-view","content":"A call's progress: phase, characters streamed so far, an estimated token count (characters ÷ 4), the current speed, accounts asked","locale":"en"},"8444":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-148","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-live-view","content":"`finished`","locale":"en"},"8445":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-149","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-live-view","content":"A call ended, with its full record and the updated totals for today","locale":"en"},"8446":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-150","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-live-view","content":"`ping`","locale":"en"},"8447":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-151","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-live-view","content":"A heartbeat every 15 seconds when nothing else happens","locale":"en"},"8448":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-152","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-live-view","content":"Progress events go out at most 4 times a second per call; a phase change is always sent at once. With nobody subscribed, none of this costs anything.","locale":"en"},"8449":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-153","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-live-view","content":"Each subscriber may fall at most 1000 events behind. A connection that reads too slowly is closed; on reconnecting it gets a fresh `snapshot`, which replaces everything it missed.","locale":"en"},"8450":{"id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage-154","page_id":"/en/docs/advanced-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/advanced-usage#the-live-view","content":"When the server shuts down, this stream ends first so it never holds up the shutdown.","locale":"en"},"8451":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","type":"page","content":"Anthropic-compatible API","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","API reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","locale":"en"},"8452":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-0","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","content":"Reference for /v1/messages and /v1/messages/count_tokens: request validation, how native forwarding or protocol conversion is chosen, the fields and content blocks conversion supports, thinking-signature replay, effort mapping, stream events, token counting and errors.","locale":"en"},"8453":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-1","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-validation","content":"Request validation","locale":"en"},"8454":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-2","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"Native forwarding or protocol conversion","locale":"en"},"8455":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-3","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding","content":"Native forwarding","locale":"en"},"8456":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-4","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#protocol-conversion","content":"Protocol conversion","locale":"en"},"8457":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-5","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"Request fields","locale":"en"},"8458":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-6","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#content-blocks","content":"Content blocks","locale":"en"},"8459":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-7","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#effort-mapping","content":"Effort mapping","locale":"en"},"8460":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-8","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#response","content":"Response","locale":"en"},"8461":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-9","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#thinking-signatures","content":"Thinking signatures","locale":"en"},"8462":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-10","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#stream-events","content":"Stream events","locale":"en"},"8463":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-11","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#token-counting","content":"Token counting","locale":"en"},"8464":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-12","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#errors","content":"Errors","locale":"en"},"8465":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-13","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#protocol-references","content":"Protocol references","locale":"en"},"8466":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-14","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","content":"These two endpoints are compatible with Anthropic Messages and serve clients such as the Anthropic SDKs and Claude Code. The base address is `http://127.0.0.1:10600` (clients add `/v1/messages` themselves), authenticated with the model API key sent as `x-api-key` or `Authorization: Bearer` (see API overview). Usage examples are in Anthropic SDK.","locale":"en"},"8467":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-15","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","content":"Method and path","locale":"en"},"8468":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-16","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"8469":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-17","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","content":"`POST /v1/messages`","locale":"en"},"8470":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-18","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","content":"Generate a reply; JSON by default, SSE with `\"stream\": true`","locale":"en"},"8471":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-19","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","content":"`POST /v1/messages/count_tokens`","locale":"en"},"8472":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-20","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","content":"Count input tokens without generating a reply","locale":"en"},"8473":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-21","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","content":"Messages is stateless: send the whole conversation every time. Hoshimi keeps no history (some native upstream features may keep state of their own). Calls are recorded on the **Usage** page with the origin `messages`.","locale":"en"},"8474":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-22","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-validation","content":"Both endpoints check the outer shape of the request first and answer `400` (in Anthropic's shape) when it fails:","locale":"en"},"8475":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-23","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-validation","content":"`model` is a non-empty string. Messages does not use the default model.","locale":"en"},"8476":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-24","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-validation","content":"`messages` is a non-empty array; each message has a string `role`, and `content` is a string or an array.","locale":"en"},"8477":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-25","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-validation","content":"`stream`, when present, is a boolean.","locale":"en"},"8478":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-26","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-validation","content":"`max_tokens` is a non-negative integer (optional for `count_tokens`).","locale":"en"},"8479":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-27","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-validation","content":"`tools`, when present, is an array.","locale":"en"},"8480":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-28","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-validation","content":"Extension fields are not checked here: native forwarding leaves them to the upstream, and protocol conversion checks them as described below.","locale":"en"},"8481":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-29","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"Hoshimi finds the provider through model routing, then looks at the accounts of that provider that can serve the model:","locale":"en"},"8482":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-30","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"If the provider has a Messages endpoint of its own for them (models whose protocol is Messages on a regular API provider, such as `anthropic` or `minimax-api`), the request is **forwarded natively**, rotating across those accounts.","locale":"en"},"8483":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-31","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"Otherwise it goes through **protocol conversion**. Dedicated providers with custom envelopes always use their own translators.","locale":"en"},"8484":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-32","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"The decision rests on each account's actual protocol and endpoint, not just a model's capability label. A native failure never quietly falls back to conversion.","locale":"en"},"8485":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-33","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"These provider options (in `providers.<id>.options`) adjust the behaviour:","locale":"en"},"8486":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-34","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"Option","locale":"en"},"8487":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-35","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"Effect","locale":"en"},"8488":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-36","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"`messages_passthrough: false`","locale":"en"},"8489":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-37","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"No native forwarding; force conversion, for a Messages provider with special requirements","locale":"en"},"8490":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-38","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"`messages_count_tokens: true`","locale":"en"},"8491":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-39","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"Use the upstream's native counting endpoint for `count_tokens`; on by default for `anthropic`, off for other providers","locale":"en"},"8492":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-40","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"`structured_outputs: true`","locale":"en"},"8493":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-41","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding-or-protocol-conversion","content":"Let the conversion path turn `output_config.format` into the upstream's structured output; enable only when the upstream and its models support it","locale":"en"},"8494":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-42","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding","content":"The body goes out unchanged except that `model` becomes the upstream model name (`count_tokens` also drops `stream`). System arrays, content order, opaque signatures, tools, cache markers, `context_management`, structured output and future fields are all left for the upstream to validate.","locale":"en"},"8495":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-43","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding","content":"The client's `anthropic-*` headers and query parameters go along. Upstream credentials come from the selected account; the key the client sent to the gateway is never forwarded. The `anthropic-beta` capabilities an OAuth account requires are merged with the client's.","locale":"en"},"8496":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-44","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding","content":"The response keeps `content-type`, `request-id`, `x-request-id`, `retry-after` (rounded up to whole seconds), `x-should-retry` and every `anthropic-*` header.","locale":"en"},"8497":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-45","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding","content":"A streaming response keeps the upstream's SSE frame by frame, unknown events, usage, signatures and pings included; Hoshimi inserts its own `ping` only between complete frames, never inside partial JSON. Non-streaming JSON is returned as it came.","locale":"en"},"8498":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-46","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding","content":"If the upstream stream ends without `message_stop` or `error`, or breaks off mid-frame, Hoshimi reports an error rather than a clean finish.","locale":"en"},"8499":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-47","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding","content":"When the client disconnects, Hoshimi closes the upstream connection; a stream that has begun is not replayed on another account.","locale":"en"},"8500":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-48","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding","content":"Upstream errors keep their status, body, request id and protocol headers (`x-should-retry`, `retry-after`, `anthropic-ratelimit-*` among them). An explicit `x-should-retry: false` from the upstream stops Hoshimi from retrying on another account.","locale":"en"},"8501":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-49","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#native-forwarding","content":"Being forwarded is not the same as being supported: an Anthropic-shaped endpoint can still reject features it does not implement, and its original error reaches the client.","locale":"en"},"8502":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-50","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#protocol-conversion","content":"The conversion path turns a Messages request into an internal Chat request, hands it to the provider's adapter, and turns the result back into Messages.","locale":"en"},"8503":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-51","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"8504":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-52","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"Handling","locale":"en"},"8505":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-53","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`system`","locale":"en"},"8506":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-54","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"A string or an array of text blocks, becoming a system message; text only","locale":"en"},"8507":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-55","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`messages[].role`","locale":"en"},"8508":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-56","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`user` or `assistant` only; a `system`-role message is refused (`Messages roles must be user or assistant; use top-level system.`)","locale":"en"},"8509":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-57","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`max_tokens`","locale":"en"},"8510":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-58","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"Must be a positive integer","locale":"en"},"8511":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-59","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`temperature`, `top_p`","locale":"en"},"8512":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-60","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"Numbers, passed through","locale":"en"},"8513":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-61","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#request-fields","content":"`top_k`","locale":"en"},"8514":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-62","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[