d":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#token-counting","content":"Authentication, quota and server errors are not hidden behind an estimate; they come back as errors.","locale":"en"},"8609":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-157","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#token-counting","content":"`max_tokens` is optional. Counting generates no reply and adds no usage record.","locale":"en"},"8610":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-158","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#errors","content":"Every error uses Anthropic's shape:","locale":"en"},"8611":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-159","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#errors","content":"A body that does not parse against the endpoint's schema: `400`, `Invalid Messages request body.`.","locale":"en"},"8612":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-160","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#errors","content":"Errors the gateway raises itself (validation, routing, conversion) use Anthropic's shape, with `error.type` following the status (see API overview).","locale":"en"},"8613":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-161","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#errors","content":"Upstream errors on native forwarding keep the upstream's status, body and protocol headers.","locale":"en"},"8614":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-162","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#errors","content":"Failures after the stream has begun arrive as an `error` event.","locale":"en"},"8615":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-163","page_id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-anthropic#protocol-references","content":"Messages HTTP reference","locale":"en"},"8616":{"id":"/en/docs/api-anthropic-164","page