url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"`response.output_item.done`","locale":"en"},"8945":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-113","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"An item ends","locale":"en"},"8946":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-114","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"`response.completed`","locale":"en"},"8947":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-115","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"The full response object, with `usage`","locale":"en"},"8948":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-116","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"`response.failed`","locale":"en"},"8949":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-117","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"The upstream failed; `response.error` says why","locale":"en"},"8950":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-118","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"Content-part events such as `response.content_part.added` are not sent, so client helpers that need them (the OpenAI Python SDK's `responses.stream()`, for one) do not work; iterate the events directly.","locale":"en"},"8951":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-119","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"`GET /v1/models`","locale":"en"},"8952":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-120","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"8953":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-121","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"Notes","locale":"en"},"8954":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-122","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"`id`","locale":"en"},"8955":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-123","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"The upstream's model name; a name several providers share is listed once (the first provider in order)","locale":"en"},"8956":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-124","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"`owned_by`","locale":"en"},"8957":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-125","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"The id of the provider that serves it","locale":"en"},"8958":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-126","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"`free`","locale":"en"},"8959":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-127","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"`true` when the station says calls are free, `false` when it says they cost, `null` when it says nothing (the usual case)","locale":"en"},"8960":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-128","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"`display_name`","locale":"en"},"8961":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-129","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"The display name; equal to `id` when unknown","locale":"en"},"8962":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-130","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"The `limit` query parameter (1–1000) returns the first `limit` models and caps the wait for providers to refresh their catalogues at two seconds: slow providers are represented by cached, configured or built-in ids while the refresh continues in the background. Claude Code's model discovery uses `?limit=1000`. Without `limit`, the full catalogue is returned.","locale":"en"},"8963":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-131","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"Model capabilities (vision, reasoning, tools, context length, effort options) are not here; see the management endpoint `GET /api/v1/models` in Management API.","locale":"en"},"8964":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-132","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-routing","content":"The `model` of a request is resolved like this:","locale":"en"},"8965":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-133","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-routing","content":"`provider/model`, where `provider` is an enabled provider id: that provider serves it, and everything after the first slash (further slashes included) is the upstream model name.","locale":"en"},"8966":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-134","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-routing","content":"Otherwise the first provider, in provider order, whose catalogue has the name.","locale":"en"},"8967":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-135","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-routing","content":"If none has it and only one provider is enabled, the name goes to that provider as is.","locale":"en"},"8968":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-136","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-routing","content":"Otherwise `404`, code `model_not_found`.","locale":"en"},"8969":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-137","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-routing","content":"When `model` is absent, `server.default_model` is used (**Settings** › **General** › **Default model**, or `hoshimi serve --default-model`).","locale":"en"},"8970":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-138","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-routing","content":"Once a provider is chosen, Hoshimi rotates and retries across its accounts. When the station answers 404/410 for a model on every account, the model is held out for a while (`503`, `model_unavailable`). See Model and account behaviour.","locale":"en"},"8971":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-139","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`reasoning_effort` (Chat) and `reasoning.effort` (Responses) follow these rules. A request without an effort level is not touched, and a caller's own `max_tokens` stays as it is.","locale":"en"},"8972":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-140","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"**Models with their own thinking menu** (the **Models** page shows several levels, for example `disabled` / `low` / `high` / `max`): a level on the menu is used as is; anything else goes through these aliases:","locale":"en"},"8973":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-141","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"Request","locale":"en"},"8974":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-142","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"Becomes","locale":"en"},"8975":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-143","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`minimal`, `light`","locale":"en"},"8976":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-144","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`low`","locale":"en"},"8977":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-145","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`balanced`","locale":"en"},"8978":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-146","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`medium`","locale":"en"},"8979":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-147","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`deep`","locale":"en"},"8980":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-148","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`high`","locale":"en"},"8981":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-149","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`xhigh`","locale":"en"},"8982":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-150","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`max`","locale":"en"},"8983":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-151","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"If the result is still not on the menu, the model's default level is used. The chosen level is written into the upstream request the way the model declares; the output ceiling is then the smaller of the model's capacity and the request's own value, whatever the level.","locale":"en"},"8984":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-152","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"**Other reasoning models** use Hoshimi's three output budgets (one ceiling shared by thinking and the answer):","locale":"en"},"8985":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-153","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"Level","locale":"en"},"8986":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-154","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"Written in the request as","locale":"en"},"8987":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-155","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai