eiling is doubled.","locale":"en"},"8998":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-166","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"The ceiling never exceeds the model's maximum output or the request's own `max_tokens`, and never drops below 512.","locale":"en"},"8999":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-167","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"For these models the `reasoning_effort` / `reasoning` fields are not sent upstream; only `max_tokens` controls the budget.","locale":"en"},"9000":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-168","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"For a model that neither reasons nor has a thinking menu, Hoshimi leaves the effort fields alone and passes them to the upstream as they are. Each model's levels and default are on the **Models** page, or in `efforts` and `effort_default` of `GET /api/v1/models`.","locale":"en"},"9001":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-169","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#classification","content":"TypeSafe classifiers are not chat models. They are not in `/v1/models` and are used through their own endpoints (with an account on the `typesafe` provider).","locale":"en"},"9002":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-170","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#classification","content":"The body sent to `POST /v1/classify`:","locale":"en"},"9003":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-171","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#classification","content":"`model` must be an id from `/v1/classifiers`; otherwise the answer is `404` (`Select a classifier from /v1/classifiers.`).","locale":"en"},"9004":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-172","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#classification","content":