docs/config-paths#schema-upgrades","content":"When the database was last used by a newer Hoshimi, an older one warns at start:","locale":"en"},"10453":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-69","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-paths#schema-upgrades","content":"The older version still runs, but some records may not show correctly. Back up the data directory before downgrading.","locale":"en"},"10454":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-70","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-paths#logs","content":"Hoshimi writes no log file: every log line goes to standard error (stderr). Once the server listens, standard output gets one line, `SERVER_READY url=http://…`, so scripts can pick up the actual address.","locale":"en"},"10455":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-71","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-paths#logs","content":"When Hoshimi runs as a system service, the service manager collects the logs (for example `journalctl`); see Installation.","locale":"en"},"10456":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-72","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-paths#move-the-configuration-file","content":"The old `--config` option and `HOSHIMI_CONFIG` environment variable have been removed. A `config.json` in the working directory is neither read nor migrated automatically. After upgrading, run:","locale":"en"},"10457":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-73","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-paths#move-the-configuration-file","content":"and move the old configuration file to the path it prints before starting the new version.","locale":"en"},"10458":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-74","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-paths#let-the-old-json-records-import-themselves","content":"Earlier versions kept usage, check-ins and probe verdicts in `stats.json`, `checkin.json` and `probe.json`. At the first start after upgrading, these files are imported into `hoshimi.db` and renamed to `*.migrated`. An unreadable one is renamed to `*.corrupt` and that record starts empty. Nothing is imported again once the database holds that kind of record.","locale":"en"},"10459":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-75","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-paths#check","content":"This confirms the configuration can be read and lists the channels and account counts that would run. Afterwards the `*.migrated` files can be deleted.","locale":"en"},"10460":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-76","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-paths#backing-up-and-resetting","content":"Task","locale":"en"},"10461":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-77","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-paths#backing-up-and-resetting","content":"How","locale":"en"},"10462":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-78","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-paths#backing-up-and-resetting","content":"Full backup","locale":"en"},"10463":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-79","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-paths#backing-up-and-resetting","content":"Stop the server and copy the whole data directory","locale":"en"},"10464":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-80","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-paths#backing-up-and-resetting","content":"Move to another machine","locale":"en"},"10465":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-81","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-paths#backing-up-and-resetting","content":"Copy the data directory, then point `HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR` at it on the new machine (or put it in the default location)","locale":"en"},"10466":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-82","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","tags":[],"type":"t