en"},"10840":{"id":"/en/docs/config-276","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#when-changes-take-effect","content":"At once","locale":"en"},"10841":{"id":"/en/docs/config-277","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#when-changes-take-effect","content":"`security.allow_origins`","locale":"en"},"10842":{"id":"/en/docs/config-278","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#when-changes-take-effect","content":"The origin check at once; the CORS response headers browsers need use the list from startup, so restart after a change","locale":"en"},"10843":{"id":"/en/docs/config-279","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#when-changes-take-effect","content":"`network`, `providers.*`","locale":"en"},"10844":{"id":"/en/docs/config-280","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#when-changes-take-effect","content":"At once, for new requests; only channels whose inputs changed are rebuilt, and streaming replies finish on their original connections","locale":"en"},"10845":{"id":"/en/docs/config-281","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#when-changes-take-effect","content":"`server.max_account_retries`","locale":"en"},"10846":{"id":"/en/docs/config-282","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#when-changes-take-effect","content":"The next time the account pool is rebuilt (any channel's accounts or options change), or after a restart","locale":"en"},"10847":{"id":"/en/docs/config-283","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#when-changes-take-effect","content":"`server.stats_keep_days`","locale":"en"},"10848":{"id":"/en/docs/config-284","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#when-changes-take-effect","content":"At the next pruning (triggered by new records, at most once a minute)","locale":"en"},"10849":{"id":"/en/docs/config-285","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#when-changes-take-effect","content":"`server.check_updates`","locale":"en"},"10850":{"id":"/en/docs/config-286","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#when-changes-take-effect","content":"At once","locale":"en"},"10851":{"id":"/en/docs/config-287","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#when-changes-take-effect","content":"`server.auto_refresh`, `server.auto_checkin`","locale":"en"},"10852":{"id":"/en/docs/config-288","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#when-changes-take-effect","content":"See the note above","locale":"en"},"10853":{"id":"/en/docs/config-289","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#when-changes-take-effect","content":"`playground.*`","locale":"en"},"10854":{"id":"/en/docs/config-290","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#when-changes-take-effect","content":"From the next message","locale":"en"},"10855":{"id":"/en/docs/config-291","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#when-changes-take-effect","content":"Changes made with `hoshimi config set` or by editing the file take effect after a server restart.","locale":"en"},"10856":{"id":"/en/docs/config-292","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#reading-and-changing-it-from-the-command-line","content":"Keys are dotted. Values are parsed as JSON when they can be (numbers, `true`/`false`, lists, objects), otherwise kept as strings. `null` (or `none`) clears a value.","locale":"en"},"10857":{"id":"/en/docs/config-293","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#reading-and-changing-it-from-the-command-line","content":"The whole configuration is validated before writing, so set keys that depend on each other in one go. To switch to proxy mode, for example, set the whole `network` object; `network.mode proxy` on its own is refused for lack of a proxy URL.","locale":"en"},"10858":{"id":"/en/docs/config-294","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#reading-and-changing-it-from-the-command-line","content":"`show` and `get` print access keys, account credentials and proxy URLs as `***`. `get` reads what the file actually contains, and a key missing from the file gives `Unknown setting`.","locale":"en"},"10859":{"id":"/en/docs/config-295","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#reading-and-changing-it-from-the-command-line","content":"Restart the server afterwards. The full command reference is in Commands.","locale":"en"},"10860":{"id":"/en/docs/config-296","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#how-the-file-is-written","content":"Each save writes a temporary file in the same folder and then replaces `config.json` atomically, so a half-written file never appears. The file holds refresh tokens in plain text, so after each save its permissions are restricted to the owner (`0600`) where the file system supports that; Windows and some network mounts do not. Treat it as a credential store and do not share a filled-in copy.","locale":"en"},"10861":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","type":"page","content":"Architecture","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-architecture","locale":"en"},"10862":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-0","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture","content":"The core / api / cli / webui layers and the layering rule, how Services is assembled and updated while running, the app factory, error mapping, and one model request from start to end.","locale":"en"},"10863":{