en"},"11485":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-93","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-setup#scriptsdevpy-tasks","content":"`test-site`","locale":"en"},"11486":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-94","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-setup#scriptsdevpy-tasks","content":"The documentation site's tests and type-check","locale":"en"},"11487":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-95","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-setup#scriptsdevpy-tasks","content":"The site tasks are covered in Documentation site. Run `python scripts/dev.py check` once before committing: it covers CI's Python and Web UI checks.","locale":"en"},"11488":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-96","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-setup#scriptsdevpy-tasks","content":"`test-py` always runs the whole suite. To run part of it, call pytest directly, for example `python -m pytest tests/core/test_registry.py -k prefixed`.","locale":"en"},"11489":{"id":"/en/docs/development-setup-97","page_id":"/en/docs/development-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-setup#clones-of-the-reference-projects","content":"To compare against upstream protocols, clone the reference repositories into the repository root (`dsh-our-free-model/`, `codex-api/`, `Hanaikada/`, `pi/`, `pi-free/`, `free-claude-code/` and so on). They are all in `.gitignore` and never committed; development, tests and builds do not need them. What each one is for is in Development.","locale":"en"},"11490":{"id":"/en/docs/development-site","page_id":"/en/docs/development-site","type":"page","content":"Documentation site","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-site","locale":"en"},"11491":{"id":"/en/docs/development-site-0","page_id":"/en/docs/development-site","tags":[],"typ