nt. Click **Save account**.","locale":"en"},"14773":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-33","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#adding-a-local-server","content":"Without `base_url` the default address is used; an account can be just an `id`.","locale":"en"},"14774":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-34","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#adding-a-local-server","content":"`base_url` must be an HTTP(S) address without a user name and password, query or fragment; `/v1` is appended when it is missing.","locale":"en"},"14775":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-35","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#adding-a-local-server","content":"When `api_key` (or `access_token`, `token`) has a value it is sent as `Authorization: Bearer`; otherwise no auth header is sent.","locale":"en"},"14776":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-36","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#adding-a-local-server","content":"Local models are never marked free (`free` is `null`).","locale":"en"},"14777":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-37","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#how-each-backend-is-handled","content":"**LM Studio**: reads the actual context length of loaded models (cached for 30 seconds). Before a request it makes a rough check: when a quarter of the messages' JSON byte size plus `max_tokens` exceeds the loaded context, it answers 400 at once (`LM Studio request exceeds this model's loaded context window`). For requests close to the limit, the server's own tokenizer still decides. Thinking levels are sent as `reasoning_effort` (`minimal` becomes `low`; `xhigh` and `max` become `high`).","locale":"en"},"14778":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-38","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#how-each-backend-is-handled","content":"**Ollama**: reads each model's capabilities, keeps only models that can do completion or tool calls, and marks vision, thinking and tool support from them; the context length is the largest one in the model info. A model whose details fail to load is still listed. Thinking levels are sent as `reasoning_effort` (`minimal` becomes `low`, `xhigh` becomes `max`).","locale":"en"},"14779":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-39","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#how-each-backend-is-handled","content":"**llama.cpp**: the thinking switch maps to chat-template parameters: `enable_thinking` and `thinking` in `chat_template_kwargs`. A request that already sets `enable_thinking` cannot also name a thinking level.","locale":"en"},"14780":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-40","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#how-each-backend-is-handled","content":"A thinking menu (including the off level `none`) appears only when the catalogue says the model thinks.","locale":"en"},"14781":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-41","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#conventional-api-services","content":"These services' addresses, protocols and catalogue endpoints are built in, so an account needs only a key.","locale":"en"},"14782":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-42","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#adding-an-account","content":"Pick the service in **Channels** and click **Add account**. The authentication method is **API key**: fill in the **API key**, and optionally **API base URL (optional)** and **Model IDs**; OpenAI, xAI and Vercel AI Gateway also offer a **Protocol** choice. Some services also support browser or device-code sign-in:","locale":"en"},"14783":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-43","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-lo