se channels correspond to the free, trial or subscription allowances of AI coding tools and platforms. Most of these stations do not hand out an API key you can paste; they issue tokens through a browser sign-in. Hoshimi performs the sign-in in place of the official client, stores the credential as an account, and takes care of renewal and check-in.","locale":"en"},"15193":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-20","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations","content":"This page describes what Hoshimi's adapters implement. Each station decides its own free allowance, models and rules, and can change them at any time; the built-in model lists are only a fallback for when the station's listing cannot be reached. What actually works is whatever the station answers now.","locale":"en"},"15194":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-21","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"Open **Channels** and pick the station from the list (stations without accounts are under the **Not set up** filter).","locale":"en"},"15195":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-22","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"Click **Sign in**. The dialog goes through **Request a link**, **Finish in the browser** and **Signed in**, and opens the station's login page in a new tab.","locale":"en"},"15196":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-23","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"For device-code stations, the dialog shows a **Verification code**; enter it on the authorization page.","locale":"en"},"15197":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-24","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"When the browser is not on the machine running Hoshimi, paste the address the browser finally lands on into **Authorization code or callback URL** and click **Submit code**.","locale":"en"},"15198":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-25","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"On success it prints `Signed into <channel> as <account id>.` and the account is written to `config.json`.","locale":"en"},"15199":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-26","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"A sign-in waits at most 10 minutes. In the Web UI you can cancel it; a callback that arrives after cancelling does not save an account.","locale":"en"},"15200":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-27","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"Signing in again as the same station identity updates the existing account rather than adding another.","locale":"en"},"15201":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-28","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"Stations that need a local callback listen only on `127.0.0.1` (or `localhost`) for the duration of the sign-in, never on a public interface. When the browser is on another machine, paste the callback with `--manual` or the Web UI's **Authorization code or callback URL**. The one flow without manual input (Loomy) has to be finished in a browser on the same machine.","locale":"en"},"15202":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-29","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#at-a-glance","content":"Channel","locale":"en"},"15203":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-30","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#at-a-glance","content":"Station","locale":"en"},"15204":{"id":"/en/d