`."],[11653,"A `Services` whose `fake` provider is declared in the configuration, so a settings save rebuilds the pool as it was; providers in `extra` join the pool as `fake0`, `fake1`"],[9376,"A `tool` event with `status` `waiting` asks for an answer. Send it with the step's `id`:"],[15487,"A bare model ID goes to the first channel that lists it, in this fixed order: `cline`, `opencode`, `kilo`, `gemini`, `zcode`, `minimax`, `trae`, `qoder`, `qodercn`, `buddy`, `workbuddy`, `codearts`, `loomy`, `raccoon`, `lobsterai`, `eac`, `agg`, `zhipu`, `nvidia`, then every other channel."],[7920,"A bare model id: the first channel, in the built-in channel order (`cline`, `opencode`, `kilo`, `gemini`, `zcode`, `minimax`, `trae`, `qoder`, …), whose catalogue lists it."],[11015,"A bare model name: the first provider, in provider order (`PROVIDER_ORDER`), whose catalogue has it."],[8591,"A block begins: `text`, `thinking`, `redacted_thinking` or `tool_use`"],[8595,"A block ends"],[8025,"A body that also talks about quota, rate limits, balance, login or credentials does not count; `401`, `402`, `429` and `5xx` never count, whatever the body says."],[8611,"A body that does not parse against the endpoint's schema: `400`, `Invalid Messages request body.`."],[8219,"A browser made a write request from another origin. Add that origin to `security.allow_origins` (needs a tool access key)"],[9494,"A browser's CORS preflight (`OPTIONS` with `Origin` and `Access-Control-Request-Method`) needs no key; the real request that follows is checked as usual."],[8445,"A call ended, with its full record and the updated totals for today"],[8441,"A call started"],[12146,"A call that must ask you stops with **Needs approval**, opens, and shows what it would do (the command, or each file the patch changes, as a diff) and a question:"],[12096,"A call that names no shell runs in **Settings › Tools › How tools run › Shell** (`playground.shell`). **Automatic**, the default, is bash, or `sh` where there is no bash; on Windows it is PowerShell, or cmd without it. The option shows what it is now (\"Now bash\"). The menu lists only the shells installed on the machine; a chosen shell that is not installed falls back to automatic. The tool descriptions tell the model the default shell and the ones installed, and a command's result says which shell it ran in."],[9375,"A call that was stopped while running also has `\"cancelled\": true`. When the conversation is sent to a model again, each round becomes its steering messages, an assistant message with its `tool_calls`, and a `tool` message per call; with no tools on, the calls and their results go as text."],[12161,"A call waits 10 minutes for an answer; no answer counts as a denial. Stopping the reply stops a waiting call."],[8443,"A call's progress: phase, characters streamed so far, an estimated token count (characters ÷ 4), the current speed, accounts asked"],[12505,"A change made from the command line needs a server restart. To upgrade, see Installation:"],[11906,"A change users can see updates this site's pages in the same commit, in both languages."],[14835,"A channel sends with its service's default protocol: Chat Completions for most, Responses for `openai`, `meta`, `xai` and `codex`, Anthropic Messages for `anthropic`, `minimax-api`, `minimax-cn` and `vercel-ai-gateway`. \"Multi\" channels choose per model:"],[8230,"A channel that never fetched successfully uses its built-in fallback list, whose models are not guaranteed to work."],[10285,"A channel with an explicit policy **replaces** the global one; the two are not merged. A channel with `{\"mode\": \"auto\"}`, for example, reads the environment even when the global mode is `proxy`."],[10284,"A channel with no `network`, or with `{\"mode\": \"inherit\"}`, uses the global policy."],[14824,"A channel-level model declaration, used when an account has no `models`."],[10286,"A channel's `network` object without `mode` means `inherit`."],[15490,"A channel's accounts are used in the order they are configured. When a request meets an account-level failure, the gateway retries on the next account, asking at most `server.max_account_retries` accounts per request (default 3):"],[12716,"A channel's own switch and network route are not here but in that channel's details on the Channels page."],[12630,"A chat is a tree: editing a question or retrying a reply adds a new version beside the old one, and both stay readable."],[12584,"A chat whose reply is working now shows a spinner after its title (**Working…**), whether the page follows it or it works in the background; one whose tool call waits for your approval shows a shield (**Needs approval**) instead. Open it to answer."],[12173,"A check with the time"],[12646,"A compaction that fails leaves the conversation as it was. Editing a question from before a compaction, or branching from there, goes back to the whole conversation."],[9724,"A component that is not installed shows `not installed` in the table and `null` in JSON."],[9110,"A conversation is a tree of messages. Each message names the one it follows (`parent_id`, `null` for the first), so an edit or a retry adds a sibling beside the old message instead of replacing it. `current_leaf` is the last message of the path on screen; the path from the first message to it is what a model is sent."],[12641,"A conversation is compacted:"],[14797,"A Copilot token minted from the GitHub token, minted again on renewal; the inference address comes from the token"],[8021,"A credential, network or server failure; nothing is known about the model"],[12445,"A credential, network or station error that says nothing about the model"],[7816,"a custom relay needs either `signing_secret` (worker) or `access_token` (direct);"],[7837,"A custom relay without a credential"],[12430,"A default round probes the channels whose lists cannot say: OpenCode Zen, `agg` aggregator accounts and NVIDIA NIM (the ones enabled). Kilo's free list is already filtered upstream and is not part of the default round."],[8748,"A disabled provider is switched back on. The account goes into both the config file and the running pool."],[9765,"A dotted key, such as `server.port`"],[9772,"A dotted key, such as `server.port` or `security.allow_cidrs`; missing levels in between are created"],[8603,"A failure in the stream, in Anthropic's error shape"],[12428,"A failure never empties the list: the last successful catalogue stays. A failure is not retried by itself; click **Retry** (or the refresh button at the right of the toolbar) to load the catalogue again. When a station's list suddenly shrinks to less than half, the gateway keeps the old list until the next listing confirms the shrink. More in Models and reasoning effort."],[8363,"A few rules:"],[12922,"A few settings are only in `config.json`, such as `server.check_updates` (whether to ask PyPI for new versions) and the options in `providers.<id>.options` other than the network route and the Cline login method. Change them with `hoshimi config set` and restart the server:"],[12189,"A file's lines beside their numbers, highlighted, with which lines they are (**Lines 1–2000 of 5000**); a directory's folders and files, and how many more were left out"],[12127,"A fixed policy, adapted from the automatic review (\"guardian\") in OpenAI Codex. It tells the reviewer there is no sandbox."],[11254,"A flow receives an HTTP client and a `report` callback. The moment the station gives a browser address, the flow must call `report(url)`: the command line prints it and opens a browser, the API hands it to the Web UI, and neither needs to know whether the station used a device code, an external login link or a local callback port. The flow then blocks until the credential is ready and returns the account dictionary the provider understands; on failure it raises `LoginError`, whose message is shown to the user as is."],[13382,"A free mark describes the station's price list; it does not promise that an account has allowance or that a call will succeed."],[8140,"A free marker promises neither available credits nor access for every key. When a station's limited-time offer ends, a marker can go stale, but only in the direction of a missing badge, never of a wrong promise."],[8413,"A future or malformed date is a 400. `GET /api/v1/stats/days` lists every date with usage, for marking a calendar."],[8384,"A generation window under 250 milliseconds, or a speed above 250 tokens a second, counts as unmeasurable: that call's `tps` is `null` and it is left out of averages, so a rate that could not be measured never looks fast."],[7831,"A GitHub login was started for a direct relay"],[8447,"A heartbeat every 15 seconds when nothing else happens"],[11404,"A Hoshimi development setup has two parts: a Python environment with Hoshimi installed editable together with its development dependencies, and bun to install, build and test the Web UI and this documentation site. Everyday tasks run through `scripts/dev.py`, which uses only the standard library, behaves the same on Linux, macOS and Windows, and runs the same tools CI runs."],[9766,"A key that does not exist gives `Unknown setting: <KEY>` and exit code 4. A whole section can be read too:"],[10509,"A key that is not set leaves its surface open."],[9780,"A key typed on the command line stays in your shell history; use the Web UI to set it if that matters."],[12069,"A line longer than 500 characters is cut; one read returns at most 60,000 characters and says where to go on."],[11831,"A list that can grow without bound scrolls inside itself instead of stretching the page into an endless column"],[7875,"A little: one `ping` per model, at most 64 tokens, at most 2 at a time. By default only `opencode`, `nvidia` and `agg` are probed, the channels whose lists cannot tell availability; you can also probe specific models only."],[8250,"A login not finished within 10 minutes times out (for example `Login timed out waiting for authorization`); start again."],[11533,"A Lucide icon name in PascalCase (such as `Rocket`, `Terminal`, `Settings`)"],[12378,"A malformed pair counts as \"quota header unreadable\". Readings are kept in memory only, and the interface shows the header names, never their raw values."],[8281,"A malformed proxy URL in the environment makes requests fail rather than being ignored."],[11289,"A manual Release run"],[11384,"A manual run of the **Release** workflow in Actions runs the same checks and build first. Its `publish` input is off by default, which produces checked files only (download the `distributions` artifact to look at them); switch it on and run it on `main`, `hoshimi_main` or a tag to publish."],[7992,"A menu model that still has no matching level after this mapping uses its default level; a ladder model given an unknown level uses `balanced`."],[11552,"A Mermaid diagram that follows the site's light or dark theme"],[9391,"A message queued when the reply stops or fails is never read."],[12201,"A message sent just as the model finishes keeps the reply going for one more round, to answer it."],[9298,"A message sent with `/steer`, now read by the model: a `user` step with the `id` the steer was given"],[9596,"A Messages stream opens the upstream before sending headers, so authentication and rate-limit failures still carry their real status. While waiting on the upstream, Messages streams and the live usage stream send an `event: ping` (`data: {\"type\":\"ping\"}`) every 15 seconds, only ever between complete events."],[10027,"A model API key is set but not sent, or a stale `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` overrides `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`"],[10063,"A model API key is set, but the variable named by `env_key` is empty or wrong"],[15154,"A model being listed does not prove there is quota for it or that inference will succeed. `nvidia` takes part in the default availability probe, so you can confirm with one real request from the **Models** page or `POST /api/v1/probe`; see Model behaviour. Capabi