all record is cleared; this cannot be undone. Calls in flight are still recorded when they end."],[8703,"Every date with usage"],[9782,"Every environment variable Hoshimi reads: its own HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR and HOSHIMI_LOG_LEVEL, the standard variables behind the default data folder and proxies, the credential variables the cloud SDKs read, the variables set for the Playground's commands, and the ones it deliberately ignores."],[8610,"Every error uses Anthropic's shape:"],[12714,"Every field **saves on its own** as it changes; there is no overall save button. Switches and selections save at once, text and number fields when you leave them (or press Enter), and list fields each time a value is added or removed. A save shows **Saved**; a field that needs a restart shows **Saved · Takes effect after a restart.** An invalid value shows the reason and leaves the configuration unchanged."],[9606,"Every hoshimi command: what it does, its arguments and options with their defaults, its output, the --json fields and examples, taken from each command's --help and the source."],[11592,"Every kind of check in Hoshimi: the pytest layout and shared fixtures, how provider and route tests are written, the Web UI's Vitest rule tests, the generated-type check, check_layout.py for sideways overflow in real browsers, and how CI runs them."],[8177,"Every log line (written to stderr; there is no log file). `HOSHIMI_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG hoshimi serve` or `hoshimi serve --debug` adds detail"],[12699,"Every model call the Playground makes is recorded in Usage like any other call, under its own origin: `playground` for replies, `playground-title` for titles, `playground-vision` for image descriptions, `playground-compact` for compaction summaries and `playground-review` for automatic reviews of tool calls."],[12639,"Every model has a **context window**: how much of a conversation it can read at once. The ring beside the send button shows how much of it is left; press it, or type `/status`, for the details. The window is the one the model's station lists. When a station refuses a request as too long and names its real limit, that limit is used from then on."],[13072,"Every model you can call: search, abilities, context length, availability probes, and a shortcut to try one in the Playground"],[9474,"Every other path"],[11842,"Every page's root, the `.body` of `AppDialog` and `SideSheet`, and `DataTable`'s `.row` use `var(--app-scroll-lane)` in `padding-inline-end`"],[11057,"Every provider (a \"channel\" in the Web UI) is a `Provider` subclass in `hoshimi/core/providers/`: it holds the provider's accounts and options, knows how to send one turn upstream with one account, and turns the upstream stream into **normalized chunks**. The shared parts, account rotation, retries, cooldowns and the catalogue cache, live in the base class; an adapter writes only what is particular to its station."],[8431,"Every record has a sequence number `seq` that never repeats, even after the statistics are cleared, so it is safe as a paging cursor."],[10517,"Every request (WebSockets included) goes through these four checks in order. The first failure answers the request at once; nothing reaches upstream:"],[10241,"Every request Hoshimi sends upstream (model catalogues, inference, login, token refresh, balances, check-in) picks its route from a network policy: direct, or through a proxy. There is one global default and each channel can override it. This page shows how to write these policies, when they apply, and where to look when something fails."],[9496,"Every request passes these checks, in this order, before it reaches an endpoint. A request that fails one gets:"],[10796,"Every save (Web UI, API, `hoshimi config set`) and every start (`hoshimi serve`, `hoshimi check`) validates the whole configuration first; when it fails, the file is left as it was. The possible errors:"],[11683,"Every scrolling area in the Web UI scrolls in one direction (`.app-scroll` down, `.app-scroll-x` sideways, such as code blocks, tables and the stepper), so a sideways scrollbar anywhere else is a layout bug. The unit tests can only read the source; `scripts/check_layout.py` finds these bugs in real browsers."],[11833,"Every scrolling area scrolls through `.app-scroll`; see below"],[10946,"Every service that holds the settings object (renewal, check-in, login, update checks, the network client) is pointed at the new one, so none of them later writes the old configuration back over the file."],[10415,"Every setting and the channel accounts' credentials"],[11559,"Every statement must be backed by the code; when old documentation or memory disagrees with the code, the code wins. What cannot be confirmed is left out."],[11973,"Every station and service you can connect. The filter above switches between **All**, **In use**, **Needs attention**, **Not set up** and **Off**; choose a channel and its accounts, today's usage, allowance and network settings open beside the list, with a **Sign in** or **Add account** button"],[9575,"Every stream is Server-Sent Events (`text/event-stream`). Once the response headers are out, the status is fixed at `200`, and a later failure can only be reported inside the stream; do not judge the outcome by the status alone:"],[10278,"Every target"],[10594,"Everyday use"],[11478,"Everything CI checks: `lint`, `typecheck-py`, `test-py`, `test-web`, `typegen-check`"],[14838,"Everything else defaults to Chat. The account's `protocol` or `options.model_protocols` overrides this."],[8636,"Everything the Web UI does goes through these endpoints, and scripts can call them directly. The base address is `http://127.0.0.1:10600/api/v1`."],[8123,"Evidence"],[8821,"Exact filters; `origin` is `chat`, `responses`, `messages`, `classify`, `playground` and so on"],[10206,"Example"],[15432,"Example channel IDs"],[11055,"Example: Kilo's device-code login"],[10971,"Exception"],[11175,"Exception"],[6069,"Existing custom agg accounts continue to work."],[13835,"Exis