e which models the account serves"],[7998,"Some channels' listings are a bare list of ids that cannot say which models this egress may actually use. A probe asks each one with the smallest possible request (`ping`, at most 64 tokens)."],[12429,"Some channels' model lists are only a list of ids, which cannot say which models your network egress may actually use. Click **Probe** in the toolbar and the gateway sends each of those models the smallest possible request in the background (a `ping` with at most 64 output tokens) and records a verdict from the answer."],[12338,"Some stations hand out free credits each day, claimed by a \"check-in\". With **Settings › Automation › Daily check-in** on (the default), the gateway checks in 30 seconds after launch and looks again every 24 hours, skipping a day (Beijing time, UTC+8, which the stations agree on) that is already covered. It goes one account after another, never several stations at once, to stay clear of the stations' risk controls. Stations without a check-in are skipped."],[12997,"Source"],[13569,"Source"],[13570,"Source ID"],[11725,"Source layout"],[13568,"Source snapshots and coverage labels do not establish current live availability. See Providers for registration, plans and authentication."],[13563,"Source snapshots: pi `482c1381a`, pi-free `2da9909`, free-claude-code `f919f46d` (2026-10-19)."],[11917,"Sources of the provider definitions; the Provider inventory records their snapshots"],[12929,"Speed"],[11724,"Stack and commands"],[10381,"Standard compatible error types such as `rate_limit_error`, `insufficient_quota` and `overloaded_error` also use shared recovery. An untyped HTTP 429 is temporary throttling unless the response explicitly reports an exhausted quota."],[8632,"Start"],[12508,"Start a chat"],[12057,"Start a command that keeps running, read its output, type into it, stop it"],[12567,"Start a new chat"],[11684,"Start a server first (`hoshimi serve` or `python scripts/dev.py dev`), ideally with a co