led by its first question (up to 80 characters). Once the first reply is complete, a model names the chat in at most six words, in the language you wrote in. Which model does that is the **Title model** setting (see Playground settings below); by default it is the chat's own model. If the model cannot be reached, the first question stays the title. A title you set with **Rename** is kept."],[11976,"Until a request has gone through the gateway it says **Nothing has been served yet**. After that, tokens, cache, latency and every call by 24 hours, 7 days, 30 days, 90 days or a single day"],[10448,"Until deleted; temporary chats are deleted when left and at the next start"],[9012,"Update"],[11051,"Update the documentation"],[10866,"Updating the configuration while running"],[13158,"Upgrade"],[9394,"Upload a file first, then send its `id` in `attachment_ids`. The request body is the file itself:"],[9094,"Upload an image or a file's text"],[11367,"Uploads `dist/` as the `distributions` artifact, kept for 14 days."],[11385,"Uploads use a PyPI API token: set `TWINE_PASSWORD` in the `pypi` environment or the repository's secrets (the user name is always `__token__`). Without it, the publish job reports an error and fails."],[13405,"Upstream"],[8077,"Upstream answers often carry quota information. The gateway reads the remaining amount and the limit from the headers of inference responses, with no extra request. The first pair that parses wins, in this order:"],[8500,"Upstream errors keep their status, body, request id and protocol headers (`x-should-retry`, `retry-after`, `anthropic-ratelimit-*` among them). An explicit `x-should-retry: false` from the upstream stops Hoshimi from retrying on another account."],[8613,"Upstream errors on native forwarding keep the upstream's status, body and protocol headers."],[8245,"Upstream errors passed through the gateway keep the upstream's status code."],[13251,"Upstream key variable"],[10359,"Upstream service error"],[12319,"Usable"],[11086,"Usable without an account"],[11977,"Usage"],[12924,"Usage"],[13136,"Usage"],[10929,"Usage accounting; `stats.live` is the calls in flight"],[9924,"Usage error or invalid value (unknown option, a `config set` value that fails the checks); `check` found no enabled channel; `login` named a station without an interactive login; help shown because no command was given"],[8295,"Usage statistics"],[8635,"Usage statistics"],[10449,"Usage statistics are written in batches about once a second, and once more when the server stops; conversation messages are written as they are sent. At each start, replies that were cut off mid-stream are marked as stopped and attachments that were never sent are removed."],[9809,"Usage statistics, check-in records, probe verdicts and Playground conversations"],[10418,"Usage statistics, check-in state and history, probe verdicts, Playground conversations and attachments"],[8701,"Usage totals for one range"],[11161,"Usage, with OpenAI's field names (`prompt_tokens`, `completion_tokens`, `total_tokens`; cache hits in `prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens`)"],[12589,"Use **Add photos and files** (the `+` button), drop files anywhere on the chat, or paste them into the box. Each file uploads right away and shows in a tray above the text; remove one with its close button before sending. A message can go with attachments and no text."],[12638,"Use **Copy** on a message to copy its text, and **Copy code** on a code block to copy just the code."],[10259,"use `http`, `https`, `socks5` or `socks5h`;"],[10128,"Use `low`, `medium`, `high` and so on, or a model's own level name. Hoshimi's mapping is in OpenAI-compatible API; each model's levels are on the **Models** page."],[15152,"Use `nvidia/<model-id>` to select this channel explicitly. When the model ID itself contains a slash, the `nvidia/` prefix makes sure the request lands here rather than on an earlier channel in the routing order:"],[8103,"Use native model ids"],[13517,"Use one of three authentication methods: an API key, application default credentials (ADC), or a service-account file."],[8226,"use the `channel/model` form, such as `kilo/<model id>`;"],[13216,"Use the agg channel for any OpenAI-compatible station: give its address or one of the 22 station presets, the account fields, several stations side by side, capability declarations and free marks."],[10252,"Use the global policy; this is a channel's default"],[15499,"Use the matching cloud platform channel for enterprise cloud accounts, and LM Studio, Ollama or llama.cpp for models on your own machine."],[8491,"Use the upstream's native counting endpoint for `count_tokens`; on by default for `anthropic`, off for other providers"],[7805,"Used"],[8388,"Used for"],[11257,"Used for"],[11540,"Used for"],[11909,"Used for"],[10431,"Used only when `playground.workspace` is empty"],[12726,"Used when a request does not name a model. Searchable; **None** means a request must name its model"],[7982,"Used when the menu has it"],[7985,"Used when the menu has it"],[8550,"User messages"],[7560,"User-Agent"],[15326,"User-Agent"],[13530,"Uses Bedrock ConverseStream. Every authentication method needs `hoshimi[bedrock]`."],[8661,"Validate and append an account"],[9675,"Validate the configuration and report which channels and accounts would be served, without starting the server."],[10963,"Validates the security settings; on a problem it raises `ValidationError` and the server does not start."],[10574,"Validation"],[9857,"Value"],[9950,"Value"],[10083,"Value"],[10148,"Value"],[12957,"Value"],[9793,"Variable"],[9831,"Variable"],[9856,"Variable"],[10003,"Variable"],[9791,"Variables Hoshimi does not read"],[9789,"Variables read by the cloud SDKs"],[9790,"Variables set for the Playground's commands"],[5562,"Venice AI"],[13328,"Venice AI"],[8138,"Venice lists some models at a price of 0, but requires a positive account balance and answers HTTP 402 to an unfunded key, so a zero price there is not taken as free."],[370,"Ven